---
term: Common interest
section: building-blocks
order: 10
definition: The shared purpose around which a corporation forms and that its charter exists to pursue.
seeAlso:
  - higher-order-common-interest
  - jurisdiction
---
Any common interest can form a charter, whether it's economic, professional, territorial, cultural, environmental, familial, or scientific. The common interest sets the corporation's legitimate scope. Actions outside that scope lack authority under the charter.
